  "id": "organization",
  "term": "organization",
  "definition": "Organization is a more or less systematic arrangement of separate parts into a whole that serves some function. In psychological use, as in mental organization, it refers to the ordered patterning of mental life and suggests a looser, more externally dependent unity than an organism.",
